<section>
  <h1>If you find a match</h1>
  <p>
    A match is the start of an inquiry, not its conclusion. This page covers
    <a href="#employers">an organisation whose hire or applicant matches</a>
    and <a href="#listed">a person who finds their own details listed here</a>.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="employers">If a hire or an applicant matches</h2>
  {% set disclaimer = {
    title: "Not legal advice",
    body: 'This page summarises public guidance. An organisation acting on a match should involve its own legal counsel.'
  } %}{% include "partials/disclaimer.njk" %}

  <ol class="steps">
    <li class="card step" id="employers-what-a-match-means">
      <span class="step__number">1</span>
      <h3 class="step__title">Read what the match establishes</h3>
      <p>
        An indicator is a value a cited source reported in connection with DPRK
        activity, not a finding about its holder. It may belong to a victim or
        be a coincidence; the <a href="/glossary/#labels">labels</a> show how
        strongly the source put it.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="card step" id="employers-check-the-source">
      <span class="step__number">2</span>
      <h3 class="step__title">Check it against the cited source</h3>
      <p>
        Confirm the cited record says what the entry says about the same value.
        If it does not, report it by <a href="/submit/">submission email</a>.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="card step" id="employers-preserve-evidence">
      <span class="step__number">3</span>
      <h3 class="step__title">Preserve evidence, and do not alert the person yet</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The FBI&rsquo;s {% set externalLink = { url: "https://www.ic3.gov/PSA/2024/PSA240516", text: "announcement of 16 May 2024" } %}{% include "partials/external-link.njk" %} recommends evaluating the suspect&rsquo;s network activity.</li>
        <li>SEAL&rsquo;s {% set externalLink = { url: "https://frameworks.securityalliance.org/dprk-it-workers/mitigating-dprk-it-workers", text: "guidance on mitigating DPRK IT workers" } %}{% include "partials/external-link.njk" %} advises against ending the engagement abruptly.</li>
        <li>The FBI&rsquo;s {% set externalLink = { url: "https://www.ic3.gov/PSA/2025/PSA250123", text: "announcement of 23 January 2025" } %}{% include "partials/external-link.njk" %} notes that discovered workers have held stolen data for ransom.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li class="card step" id="employers-involve-counsel">
      <span class="step__number">4</span>
      <h3 class="step__title">Bring in counsel, HR and security together</h3>
      <p>
        The {% set externalLink = { url: "https://ofac.treasury.gov/media/923126/download", text: "May 2022 State, Treasury and FBI guidance" } %}{% include "partials/external-link.njk" %} warns of legal consequences, including
        sanctions designation, for involvement in DPRK IT-worker activity.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="card step" id="employers-verify">
      <span class="step__number">5</span>
      <h3 class="step__title">Verify the person, not only the value</h3>
      <p>
        The same guidance recommends verifying employment and education history
        through independently found contacts.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li class="card step" id="employers-report">
      <span class="step__number">6</span>
      <h3 class="step__title">Report it</h3>
      <p>
        In the United States, report to the {% set externalLink = { url: "https://www.ic3.gov/", text: "Internet Crime Complaint Center (IC3)" } %}{% include "partials/external-link.njk" %} or the local FBI field
        office. Elsewhere, use the national cyber security authority. The
        <a href="/sources/#reporting">reporting list</a> gathers these
        documents.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h3 id="fair-treatment">Fair treatment</h3>
  <p>
    Screening must rest on verifiable conduct and documents, never on
    nationality, ethnicity, name, accent or appearance. Many
    <a href="/remote-workers/red-flags/">red flags</a> are common among genuine
    hires.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 id="listed">If you are listed on this site</h2>

  <h3 id="listed-why">Why a real person&rsquo;s details can appear</h3>
  <p>
    The operators use stolen and borrowed names, documents, photographs and
    accounts, so your details can appear without any involvement on your part.
  </p>

  <h3 id="listed-what-an-entry-says">What an entry does and does not say</h3>
  <p>
    An indicator entry says only that a cited source reported the value in
    connection with DPRK activity. See the <a href="/about/#disclaimer">disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h3 id="listed-request">How to ask for a correction or removal</h3>
  <p>
    Use the <a href="/submit/">submission email</a>
    {%- if site.repoUrl %} or open an issue on the
    {% set externalLink = { url: site.repoUrl + "/issues", text: "GitHub repository" } %}{% include "partials/external-link.njk" %}
    {%- endif %}.
    {%- if site.businessEmail and "TODO" not in site.businessEmail %}
    A request that should not be public can be sent to
    <a href="mailto:{{ site.businessEmail }}">{{ site.businessEmail }}</a>.
    {%- endif %}
    Include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>the address of the page and the identifier as it appears there;</li>
    <li>what is wrong, such as a stolen identity or a value the source did not print;</li>
    <li>a link to a public record that supports the correction, if one exists.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Do not send identity documents; email is not a secure channel.</p>

  <h3 id="listed-what-happens">What happens to a request</h3>
  <p>
    A person reads every request. An entry its cited source does not support is
    corrected or withdrawn. Copies already taken, including search engine
    caches, are outside the site&rsquo;s control.
  </p>

  <p id="listed-government-records">
    Where an entry rests on an indictment, sanctions designation or wanted
    notice, contest the record with the issuing authority; the site corrects
    only its own misstatements.
  </p>
</section>
